Backport JDK-8281440: AWT: Conversion from string literal loses const qualifier

A string literal is const, and the windows AWT code assigns them to LPTSTR,
LPWSTR and char* in twenty places. cl.exe allows that; clang refuses it:

  awt_PrintControl.cpp:1054: error: cannot initialize a variable of type
  'LPTSTR' (aka 'wchar_t *') with an rvalue of type 'const wchar_t *'

The failing build named two lines in one file, but they are one instance of a
class upstream already swept in a single commit, so take the whole sweep rather
than meet the other eighteen one build at a time. Where the value really is
handed to an API that wants a mutable pointer the fix is a cast, and where it
is only read it becomes const.

Upstream: https://bugs.openjdk.org/browse/JDK-8281440

